summary: This file sets up one background program. web runs a Node.js app and starts with supervisord.

[program:web] program="web"
  1 section [program:web]
    => Starts a program section. Visor and supervisorctl call it web.
  2 key     command=node server.js
    => What it runs: a Node.js app.
  3 key     stopsignal=INT
    => Stops it with the INT signal (the default is TERM).
  3 unset   not set: autostart, autorestart, stdout_logfile, stderr_logfile
    => Defaults apply: it starts with supervisord, it’s restarted only if it exits with an unexpected code and its output and errors go to files supervisord names itself.
    suggest: Files supervisord names itself are hard to find and are deleted when supervisord restarts. Set both log paths.
    add: stdout_logfile=/usr/local/var/log/supervisor/web.log
    add: stderr_logfile=/usr/local/var/log/supervisor/web.err.log
